-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A: NORM-LOG §7 T4, with the party-qualified read.
-- Pass: in both orders the borrow at 20 is blocked (the MAY stays waiting) because the return was due at 14
-- and settling writes overdue before the borrow is matched. Before A only loan RAND borrowing blocked it.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF patron
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF giveBack, payFine, borrow
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
loan MEANS
  PARTY patron MUST giveBack WITHIN 14
  HENCE FULFILLED
  LEST  RECORD `overdue` IS TRUE HENCE (PARTY patron MUST payFine WITHIN 7)
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
borrowing MEANS
  PARTY patron MAY borrow PROVIDED RECALL patron's `overdue` EQUALS NOTHING WITHIN 100
#TRACE loan RAND borrowing AT 0 WITH PARTY patron DOES borrow AT 20
#TRACE borrowing RAND loan AT 0 WITH PARTY patron DOES borrow AT 20
